	abstract = {Introduction – With the growing digitalization, the demand of consumers has witnessed a paradigm shift from just a product to the experience associated with the purchase. A significant shift toward a cashless and digital payment system was seen in business strategy and management at the beginning of the twenty-first century. Digitalization of payment systems in India is an important area of increasing interest for any industry. Purpose – The aim of this chapter is to empirically examine the impact of digital payment systems in the hospitality industry on customer satisfaction. The study will cover various aspects of technological acceptance of digital payment methods. Design/methodology/approach – The conceptual model along with the structured questionnaire will be framed based on the study objectives. An online/offline survey was conducted, and the collected responses were analyzed with the help of PLS-SEM version 4.0.9.6. Findings – The results revealed that the technological acceptance of digital payments systems puts a significant impact on customer satisfaction in the hospitality sphere. Impact/Outcome – The study added valuable knowledge towards better understanding of the applicability and advancements of digital payments systems in the arena of hospitality business based on technological acceptance. It is advised that all the stakeholders in this sector must be well versed with the nuances of technological development and must adopt them in their business. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
