	abstract = {In the contemporary financial landscape, marked by rapid technological progress and expanding mobile network coverage, cashless banking services have become an indispensable conduit for extending banking amenities to customers. However, there remains a gap in identifying the specific service quality elements that could be further optimized for improved customer experience. To bridge this gap, this study was conducted to explore and analyze the various dimensions of cashless banking service quality. Drawing on responses from 173 participants, factor analysis was employed to identify the key components of service quality that significantly influence customer satisfaction. Subsequent regression analysis confirmed that these identified factors significantly and positively impact customer satisfaction. The findings offer valuable insights for banks, suggesting targeted areas for improving service quality to enhance customer satisfaction in the realm of cashless transactions. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
