	affiliations = {Bina Nusantara University, Department of Management, Jakarta, Indonesia},
	abstract = {Green Banking is a broad word that refers to bank operations and policies that are sustainable in economic, environmental, and social dimensions. This refers to specific banking actions and practices that assist in reducing total external carbon emissions as well as internal carbon footprint. One example is the growing trend of cashless payments using mobile app services. This study investigates the effects of green banking, green image, and bank trust on bank loyalty. This is an explanatory study that employs a quantitative approach and survey methodology. With a total of 183 respondents, the sampling strategy employed was simple random sampling. This study employed the Structural Equation Modeling analysis approach with the SmartPLS 3.0 analysis tool. A statistical method used to analyze the complex relationships between variables in an integrated model. Green banking, green image, and bank trust were found to have a substantial impact on bank loyalty. This research suggested factors to be improved, such as green banking, green image, and bank trust to continue adapting to customer needs. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
