	affiliations = {Russian Presidential Academy of National Economy and Public Administration, Moscow, Russian Federation},
	abstract = {The goal of the research is to develop new scenario of the world financial system architecture on the basis of the historical experience of applying new tokens of value. Methodology: historical evolution method with account of bifurcation points and scenario development determinants. Results: Different tokens of value have different exchange mechanisms that can be observed in differences between monetary aggregates of different countries and changes in world currency system. Countries common features include legally imposed order of tokens of value emission and circulation that enables the states to use financial system as one of the instruments of regulating public production. As the humanity develops new tokens of value appear. The article touches in more details upon Tulipmania and monetary reform in Russia in 1921–1924 as possible bifurcation points of potential changes in payment systems. According to the first scenario the new currency failed. According to the second scenario old tokens of value were replaced by new ones. The choice of the development scenarios is determined by the government support regarding to new tokens of value. Taking it into consideration we carried out the analysis of crypto currencies perspectives as one of the directions of developing new architecture of the world financial system. The article observes crypto currencies evolution process and intensifying state regulation causing emerging of national gold-backed crypto currencies. Conclusions/recommendations: Historical experience shows that sustainability of the new tokens of value is provided by the state only by taking risks of their launching including measures aimed at regulating public production and limiting public expenditures. Emerged tokens of value (digital currencies) must have several levels: the first one making up the basis for new payment systems in the form of national gold-backed crypto currencies; and the second one being emitted by private entities that will become a kind of financial instruments. Creating such a system implies concluding cross-governmental agreements determining emission and circulation of new tokens of value. Changing the conventional order affecting economic interests of contracting states lead and will lead to forming a new harmonious system of by means of ruining the old one, and the outcome will depend on effectiveness of the concluded global treatments. © 2019 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
