	abstract = {Cashless payments are on the rise as technology advancements enable new and more convenient ways of payment. With the decrease in cash payments and an increased ease of paying online or by credit card, consumers do not feel the "pain of paying" anymore. Certain situations might tempt consumers to adverse impulse purchases. Many applications already leverage user profiles to create individual experiences tailored to the user. Knowing the user's current context can be used by a system to detect anomalies in behavior and warn the user. We propose a family of systems that evaluate purchase intentions based on the current user situation. The user will be notified about adverse impulse purchases and unusual behavior, so that s/he can cancel these transactions. The paper illustrates a possible system design along with corresponding use cases. © 2018 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
