	abstract = {Compared with other administrations, the Deutsche Bundespost (DBP) did not decide until 1983 in favour of card applications in telecommunications. On account of the marginal conditions existing in the Federal Republic of Germany there was no need to do so at an earlier date. Meanwhile the cashless payment of goods and services has more and more taken effect on the market. Studies, field trials and market research conducted by the DBP have documented considerable advantages and manifold application possibilities of chip cards for existing and new services. The concentration and coordination of experts of the DBP and from the German industry yielded impressive and standard-setting results. In the field of card technology, not only knowledge was gained about the characteristics of card systems, but also ideas and developments were put into practice. An example of this is the realization of the multifunctional card for public card telephones and for the mobile telephone service. A short description of some projects shows the diversity of applications of chip card technology. © 2003 Elsevier Science B.V., Amsterdam. All rights reserved.},
